{
  "an3.127:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.127 ",
  "an3.127:0.2": "13. Kusinārā ",
  "an3.127:0.3": "With Hatthaka ",
  "an3.127:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an3.127:1.2": "Then, late at night, the glorious godling Hatthaka, lighting up the entire Jeta’s Grove, went up to the Buddha. Thinking, ",
  "an3.127:1.3": "“I will stand before the Buddha,” he sank and melted down, and wasn’t able to stay still. ",
  "an3.127:1.4": "It’s like when ghee or oil is poured on sand, it sinks and melts down, and can’t remain stable. ",
  "an3.127:1.5": "",
  "an3.127:1.6": "",
  "an3.127:2.1": "Then the Buddha said to Hatthaka, ",
  "an3.127:2.2": "“Hatthaka, manifest a solid incarnation.” ",
  "an3.127:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” replied Hatthaka. He manifested a solid incarnation, bowed to the Buddha, and stood to one side. ",
  "an3.127:2.4": "The Buddha said to him, ",
  "an3.127:3.1": "“Hatthaka, I wonder whether you still promulgate now the teachings that you promulgated when you were a human being?” ",
  "an3.127:3.2": "“I still promulgate the teachings that I promulgated as a human being. ",
  "an3.127:3.3": "And I also promulgate teachings that I didn’t promulgate as a human being. ",
  "an3.127:3.4": "Just as the Buddha these days lives crowded by monks, nuns, laymen, and laywomen; by rulers and their chief ministers, and monastics of other religions and their disciples, ",
  "an3.127:3.5": "so I live crowded 